roven quick correct decisions outweigh B's unknown decision quality, and his excellent attention supports accuracy. The communication issues are concerning but may be trainable. So I could change my vote to Candidate C.\n\nLet's do that: state my current recommendation is Candidate C, because of decision quality and attention, and because B lacks evidence on those criteria. Mention concerns about C's communication and egocentric attitude, but still overall fit.\n\nNow produce public message: reference Agent 2's earlier recommendation and the lack of evidence. Provide facts: C can make correct decisions quickly; C has excellent attention skills; C difficulty communicating ideas; C regarded as egocentric; C not willing to further education. Explain implications.\n\nNow produce metadata vote: Candidate C."}
